			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1750532">
									

<p>That's what I'm seeing. It's a very interesting use of the containment build-up approach; that is, a lot of great SCPs are interesting because you read the containment procedures and wonder &quot;What the hell does it have to be to require that?&quot;, drawing you further into the article. Here, the twist is that the containment procedures essentially <em>are</em> the SCP - the Foundation tried to contain so hard, it made an anomaly.</p>
<p>Unfortunately, I think the build-up is too heavy in scientific jargon and detailed description for the payoff in the twist. Neutral vote.</p>

